{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And a man who takes a woman and her mother — it is depravity, they shall be burned with fire</b>, etc. From where do we derive [the law for] one who lies with her daughter, her son's daughter, and her daughter's daughter? It is derived by a gezerah shavah of זמה — זמה: it is written here regarding punishment, ״ואיש אשר יקח את אשה ואת אמה זמה היא״ etc., and it is written there in the warning, ״ערות אשה ובתה לא תגלה, את בת בנה ואת בת בתה לא תקח לגלות ערותה שארה הנה זמה היא״. Just as זמה there means her daughter, her son's daughter, and her daughter's daughter, so too זמה here means her daughter, her daughter's daughter, and her son's daughter — one who lies with any one of them is punished by burning. And from where do we derive that [a man] is judged regarding the relations derived from himself [i.e., his own daughter/granddaughters] just like the relations derived from her? It is derived by הנה — הנה, by a gezerah shavah of זמה — זמה: regarding the relations derived from her, it writes הנה together with זמה, as it is written in the perashah of Aḥarei: ״ערות אשה ובתה״ etc. ״שארה הנה זמה היא״; so too the relations derived from himself — ״ערות בת בנך או בת בתך״ — in which הנה is written, it is as if זמה were written with it. Then we derive again: זמה, which we brought from שאר of hers, [we learn] from זמה written regarding punishment: ״ואיש אשר יקח את אשה ואת אמה זמה היא באש ישרפו״ etc. Just as from זמה of 'a woman and her mother' we derive her daughter, her daughter's daughter, and her son's daughter [as punishable] by burning, so too זמה which we brought regarding שאר of his — his daughter, his daughter's daughter, and his son's daughter — one who lies with any one of them is punished by burning, in the chapter Elu Hen HaNisrefin." "<b>They shall be burned — him and them.</b> It is impossible to say that his first wife is among those burned, since she was married to him lawfully. Rather, ״אשה ואמה״ written here means his mother-in-law and her mother. Another interpretation: ואתהן is as our Rabbis expounded it — [parsing] with a vav, making it as two words: את הן, meaning 'one of them,' for so they call one [thing] in Greek: הינא (hina). That is to say, the law of burning applies to both of them: if he married the daughter and lay with the mother, the mother is burned with him; and if he married the mother and lay with the daughter, the daughter is burned with him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:53.961234572Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}